\v 25 \wj But I tell you of a truth, many widows were in Israel in the days of Elias, when the heaven was shut up three years and six months, when great famine was throughout all the land;\wj* 
\v 26 \wj But unto none of them was Elias sent, save unto Sarepta, a city of Sidon, unto a woman that was a widow.\wj* 
\v 27 \wj And many lepers were in Israel in the time of Eliseus the prophet; and none of them was cleansed, saving Naaman the Syrian.\wj* 
